The '''Macaio–Xàbia high speed rail line''', marketed as the '''Pantanal''', is a {{convert|830.08|km|adj=on}} {{W|standard gauge}} {{W|railway line}} inaugurated on 8 November 1985. Designed for speeds up to {{convert|360|km/h|mph|0|abbr=on}}, it runs parallel to the west coast of [[Atlántida]] to connect the cities of [[Macaio]], [[Palmarés]], [[Aigües]], [[Navassa]] and [[Xàbia]] in 2 hours and 30 minutes.

Trains are operated by the [[Baliscan Railways Group|''Transoccidental'']] cooperative of the [[Baliscan Railways Group]], as part of the [[AVB]] service. 

